    feat(node): per-repo deploy key, pinned node runtime, sealed shared module cache (CF-003)
    
    A node could not be provisioned for a private repo and could not run the tests several Go
    repos need. What the tree now carries:
    
    - scripts/deploy_key.py + node-create.sh --deploy-key: a 0600 per-repo key with one
      generated ssh_config (IdentitiesOnly), validated before any agent is spawned, copied as a
      file (never an argv value) and deleted from the staging dir in the same round trip;
      `check` prints the single clone command. Refuses a 0644 key, a public key, an HTTPS
      remote and an unrequested rotation.
    - project-node.sh layer 40 consumes NODE_DEPLOY_KEY (process-scoped GIT_SSH_COMMAND) and
      pins core.sshCommand into that one repository. A 0644 key blocks the clone instead of
      falling back to an ambient identity.
    - scripts/install-node.sh + layer 10: provision the digest-pinned v22.22.3 runtime under
      $HOME/node-toolchain and grade the OWNED binary before any PATH runtime. The linux-x64
      digest was verified by downloading the archive (31,059,464 bytes, sha256 2e5d1356...),
      not copied from a manifest.
    - scripts/gomodcache.py + the layer-10 `go:modcache` row: seed one cache, seal it read-only,
      record its bytes. The fixture measures the property instead of asserting it: a
      GOPROXY=off rebuild from the sealed cache adds 0 bytes, a cold cache cannot build, and a
      module that was never seeded is refused with `permission denied` rather than silently
      growing the cache.
    - scripts/node_hygiene.py: layer-00 footprint admission (components + 2 GiB working room
      against free space, and the total against the resolved floor) and an orphan home/key
      reaper wired into bunker-server-install.sh --reap-orphans.
    
    Docs: specs/NODE.md (layers 00/10/40, a credentials section, disk floor, orphan reaping),
    handbook M1 §3/§5/§7/§10/§12/§13 and M5 §3/§4/§5/§7/§10/§12/§13, docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md
    §58 mapping (arms 61), README scripts inventory. Contradictions named there: layer 40's
    error message already named a deploy key that no stage injected (F1-6); layer 10 graded an
    ambient `node` it never provisioned (F1-7); the spec counted 656 MB of module cache per node
    with no mechanism behind it (F1-8); README said private clones had "no tested procedure"
    (there is now a fixture-tested procedure; the live clone is still unverified).
    
    Disclosed edits to other rows' arms, required by the larger staged set and the new section:
    selftest §35 now asserts twelve staged files (was eight), §36's escaping fixture copies the
    four new scripts, and §39's plan mapping gains a §58 row (60 -> 61 arms).
    
    Tests: python3 tests/test_node_provisioning.py -> Ran 23 tests, OK (MEASURED shared
    GOMODCACHE 2097910 bytes; sealed rebuild added 0 bytes); bash tests/selftest.sh ->
    SELFTEST: PASS with §58 green; bash -n on the four edited shell scripts; py_compile on the
    new python; gitleaks protect --staged -> no leaks.
    
    Not proven here and not claimed: a live clone of the private GitLab with a real read-only
    key from a fresh bunker node, the 11 node-dependent tests in that Go repo, and reaping a
    live server's directories. The row stays open until a live run records them.
    
